   "text": {
    "L1": "A clock has two important hands. The short hand shows the hour, and the long hand shows the minutes.",
    "L2": "The minute hand counts by fives. So the number 4 means 20 minutes, not 4 minutes.",
    "L3": "The hour is the number the short hand has just passed. Do not read the number it is coming to.",
    "L4": "In the worked example, the hour hand is just past 9 and the minute hand is on 11.",
    "L5": "Count eleven groups of five: 11 times 5 is 55. The time is 9:55.",
    "L6": "a.m. is from midnight to noon, and p.m. is from noon to midnight. So 12 noon is 12 p.m.",
    "L7": "Now check this: the hour hand is just past 8 and the minute hand points to 2. Choose the time."
   },
